values ('e0f1a2b3-4c5d-4e07-8a77-7b8c9d0e1f07', 'counterpoint', 'Counterpoint', 'Counterpoint is an advanced study of independent musical lines: how they sing, combine, imitate, invert, intensify, and create form. Students write species exercises, cantus firmi, two-voice studies, three- and four-voice textures, canons, inventions, and fugue materials while analyzing Renaissance and Baroque models. The course treats counterpoint as both discipline and musicianship: a way to hear intervals, control dissonance, shape melody, plan texture, and compose with motivic economy.');

